# The LOA parser's regression corpus is EVIDENCE, and its bytes are the
# evidence. Every fixture's SHA-256 is pinned — in `fixtures/corpus.json`
# for the six letters, and in `test/tender-notice.test.ts` for the IREPS
# notice — and those digests are computed over the file exactly as it sits
# on disk.
#
# Git's end-of-line normalisation would break that pin on any checkout
# whose platform disagrees with the one the digest was taken on: the same
# committed blob would arrive as different bytes on Windows and on Linux,
# and the pin would fail on one of them while proving nothing on the
# other. `-text` turns normalisation off for these files, so the working
# copy is byte-identical to the blob everywhere and the digest means what
# it says.
packages/loa-parser/fixtures/*.txt -text
